        <mxCell id="note" value="All original form panels remain editable in NetBeans Design. ResponsiveView fits their width, EventCards adjusts column count, and DisplayText translates stored status codes. Section and offer edits are retained when switching selections. Password toggle is a JToggleButton in LoginView.form. Registration uses a separate helper with its own password field. Passwords begin hidden, and sign-in submission hides them again. Toggling changes only echoChar, never the stored or entered password. Map selection/movement callbacks use ordinary listener interfaces. Hollow diamonds denote shared aggregation of reusable value objects; they do not claim automatic Java object deletion. Relation counts read source to target." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=15;" vertex="1" parent="1">
